fact WorkItem(id: "WI-363", description: some(value: "Operation-level provision-completeness check -- the WI-343 analog at OPERATION granularity; the named soundness companion in proposal docs/proposals/library/002-iteration-collection.md (Status/soundness: WI-343 + op-provision completeness are the companion track that makes the facts the typer trusts actually true). WI-343 (delivered) checks that a carrier asserting fact Spec[X] provides Spec required SUB-SPECS (the requires chain). It does NOT check that the carrier backs every OPERATION Spec declares. So a carrier can claim fact Stream[X] while an op (e.g. takeN/collect before WI-362) has no body anywhere -> the fact is trusted, not true; a call resolves to nothing at runtime with no load-time diagnostic. CHECK: when a sort X asserts fact Spec[...], every operation Spec declares must be backed by EITHER (a) a spec-level default on Spec -- a derivation rule (head(?s)=... :- ...) OR a default operation body (operation op(...) = ...) -- OR (b) an operation X itself supplies (carrier-refined). A declared op with neither -> load-blocking LoadError, the op-granular twin of LoadError::UnsatisfiedProviderRequires. IMPL: mirror WI-343 check_provider_requires (rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/typing.rs): enumerate Spec own operations (sorts_and_own_ops / OperationInfo), for each test for a default rule/body on Spec or a provider op on X; reuse the SortProvidesInfo snapshot; skip pure-marker/effects ops as WI-343 skips EffectsRuntime. SEQUENCING: depends WI-362 -- the stdlib must be op-complete first; turning this on as a hard error before Stream takeN/collect have bodies would error on the stdlib itself (exact WI-343/List-Iterable sequencing). REF: typing.rs check_provider_requires + LoadError; tests/include/wi343_provider_requires_test.rs family. ACCEPTANCE: a carrier claiming a spec but missing a non-defaulted op errors at load with the op named; stdlib (post WI-362) stays green; existing wi343/wi325 tests green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-362"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-03T10:10:48Z"))
